Frequency-based tables for the legacy device-tree Energy Model loader
===================================================================

A CPU node references a cost node using the existing sched-energy-costs
phandle. By default, busy-cost-data contains <capacity power> pairs; the
legacy loader scales capacity to CPUFreq frequencies as before.

Optional property on the referenced cost node:

- frequency-based: boolean. busy-cost-data instead contains <frequency power>
  pairs, with frequency in kHz and the existing per-CPU power estimates.

For frequency-based tables, the loader keeps only entries present in the
policy CPUFreq table within its hardware min/max range. It preserves the
frequency and associated power, without rescaling. The data must be sorted
by strictly increasing frequency and cover every supported CPUFreq state.
An incomplete model is rejected rather than silently rescaled or guessed.
The input may contain a union of frequency plans for several speed bins.

Example:

    CPU_COST_0: core-cost0 {
        frequency-based;
        busy-cost-data = <633600 41 902400 70 1113600 83>;
    };

The new property does not change the CPUFreq plan, clocks, voltages, CPU
capacity, or power estimates. Tables without it retain the legacy behavior.
